WEBVTT

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:08.009
<v Callum Reid>Morning, everyone. Friday, 10 July. Can you all hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:17.250
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, we can hear you. More importantly, whose new car is that in the car park? It's taking up about one and a half spaces.</v>

00:00:19.329 --> 00:00:21.780
<v Olumide Adeyemi>That's confidence, that is. Definitely not mine.</v>

00:00:22.739 --> 00:00:25.539
<v David Whitfield>Mine's the one with the permanently disappointed-looking bumper.</v>

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:35.619
<v Grace Liu>I'm more interested in the heating in the portakabin. July and it's like a sauna in here. Just having a moan, before that goes on your list.</v>

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:41.280
<v Sarah Okafor>We've got the full British summer experience, then. Wet outside, tropical inside.</v>

00:00:43.229 --> 00:00:46.729
<v Callum Reid>Right, before we become a weather podcast. Finished stuff first.</v>

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:52.840
<v David Whitfield>Yeah so, already swapped the filter on the Line 3 Screw and Barrel yesterday. That's done.</v>

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:57.820
<v Callum Reid>Lovely. Finished yesterday, not something we're carrying into today?</v>

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:00.920
<v David Whitfield>Correct. Crossed off, spanners away.</v>

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:09.120
<v Callum Reid>And I tested the fire alarm panel yesterday and it's all fine now. That one's closed as well.</v>

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:14.189
<v Grace Liu>Good, yeah. Nice to have a couple actually off the board.</v>

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:23.370
<v Callum Reid>Also, the shutdown on the boiler safety valve is cancelled now, production need it running. That shutdown isn't going ahead.</v>

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:28.900
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, cancelled, not just sliding it into later today.</v>

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:37.670
<v Fiona Doyle>One observation from me: saw the pressure on the Site Water System dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own.</v>

00:01:39.909 --> 00:01:41.659
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Recovered without anyone touching anything?</v>

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:47.280
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah. Just an observation, no work request attached to that.</v>

00:01:49.129 --> 00:01:55.780
<v Callum Reid>Grace, can you book a contractor to look at the line 3 barrel by the end of the week?</v>

00:01:56.459 --> 00:02:03.109
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, I'll book a contractor to look at the line 3 barrel. By the end of the week, agreed.</v>

00:02:04.219 --> 00:02:09.120
<v David Whitfield>That's getting the booking made, rather than saying they'll physically be here by then?</v>

00:02:11.189 --> 00:02:15.039
<v Callum Reid>Exactly. Booking made. We're not promising their attendance by that deadline.</v>

00:02:16.389 --> 00:02:20.590
<v Grace Liu>Fine, I've got that. Contractor booked by the end of the week.</v>

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:31.000
<v Fiona Doyle>While we're on contractors and suppliers, the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the GT1 Fuel Gas Valve. That's still blocked on their confirmation.</v>

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:40.430
<v Priya Raman>Hang on, is that holding up the lock-out tag-out sign-off as well, or are we talking about the existing isolation?</v>

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:50.430
<v Callum Reid>Existing isolation. I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the GT1 Fuel Gas Valve this afternoon. That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:56.729
<v Grace Liu>Cal, just so we're clear, you're not treating the unconfirmed delivery as evidence that anything's been fitted?</v>

00:02:58.909 --> 00:03:06.960
<v Callum Reid>No, absolutely not. It's the isolation sign-off this afternoon, straight away in that slot. Nothing there says the replacement's arrived or been fitted.</v>

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.719
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Right, two different things. Got you.</v>

00:03:11.449 --> 00:03:15.650
<v Callum Reid>And I'll replace the seals on the main water valve by Thursday.</v>

00:03:17.539 --> 00:03:23.139
<v David Whitfield>Callum, that's the seals on the main water valve, separate from the pressure dip Fiona mentioned?</v>

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:30.020
<v Callum Reid>Yep, separate job. Mine, by Thursday. Not turning that brief pressure dip into another action.</v>

00:03:31.289 --> 00:03:37.939
<v Priya Raman>There's also the CV01 jam and the sensor check. Those need keeping together rather than losing half of it.</v>

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:47.830
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the CV01 by the end of the week. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:53.849
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Callum, both bits with you then? Clearing the jam and checking the sensors?</v>

00:03:55.770 --> 00:04:01.370
<v Callum Reid>Both with me, yeah. One action, not just pulling the material out and calling it finished.</v>

00:04:02.469 --> 00:04:07.020
<v Fiona Doyle>Um, I'll chase the purchase order for the turbine one compressor this morning.</v>

00:04:07.439 --> 00:04:12.340
<v Callum Reid>Thanks, Fiona. Whenever you get a chance this morning; don't drop everything for it.</v>

00:04:14.229 --> 00:04:19.129
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, this morning, but fitting it round things rather than treating it as urgent.</v>

00:04:20.569 --> 00:04:24.420
<v Fiona Doyle>And I'll order spare parts for the GT2 bearing next week.</v>

00:04:26.069 --> 00:04:30.970
<v Callum Reid>Right, Fiona Doyle against the spare parts order for the GT2 bearing, next week.</v>

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:37.420
<v Fiona Doyle>That's me. Next week, not another order I've promised to get out today.</v>

00:04:37.879 --> 00:04:40.680
<v David Whitfield>Full name. That's when you know purchasing's serious.</v>

00:04:41.889 --> 00:04:46.089
<v Fiona Doyle>Or I've been called into the headteacher's office. Could go either way.</v>

00:04:46.779 --> 00:04:51.680
<v Grace Liu>What about organising the toolbox talk for the team? That still needs an owner.</v>

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:58.819
<v Callum Reid>I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team by 11am. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:05:00.779 --> 00:05:07.430
<v Sarah Okafor>Callum, by 11am is having it organised, yeah? Not saying everyone's got to have sat through it by eleven?</v>

00:05:07.899 --> 00:05:11.750
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, having it organised by 11am. That's what I'm taking on.</v>

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:20.000
<v Callum Reid>Priya, can you update the risk assessment for work on the stretch wrapper next Tuesday? Fairly important, that one.</v>

00:05:20.829 --> 00:05:28.879
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, no, I can't take that on. I haven't got the capacity, and I'd rather say now than nod and let it disappear.</v>

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:37.990
<v Callum Reid>Fair enough. Saz, can you take that instead—update the risk assessment for work on the stretch wrapper next Tuesday? Still fairly important.</v>

00:05:39.759 --> 00:05:46.410
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, I'll take it from Priya. I'll update the risk assessment for work on the stretch wrapper next Tuesday.</v>

00:05:48.079 --> 00:05:54.029
<v Grace Liu>Good, that's clear. Fairly important, and it's changed hands rather than having two people supposedly owning it.</v>

00:05:54.949 --> 00:05:56.350
<v Priya Raman>Cheers, Saz. Appreciate that.</v>

00:05:57.579 --> 00:06:04.579
<v Callum Reid>Sarah, can you do a site visit at Kestrel with the contractor by the end of the week? No rush.</v>

00:06:05.629 --> 00:06:11.579
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, I'll do the site visit at Kestrel with the contractor by the end of the week.</v>

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:16.959
<v Fiona Doyle>Just—sorry, talking over you—it's Friday, so no rush isn't pushing that into next week?</v>

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:25.300
<v Callum Reid>No, still by the end of the week. No rush as in it doesn't need to jump ahead of the urgent stuff.</v>

00:06:25.879 --> 00:06:29.730
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Fits within today, without treating it as a drop-everything visit.</v>

00:06:31.129 --> 00:06:36.029
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And same distinction on the CV01, then. End of the week, but not urgent.</v>

00:06:37.319 --> 00:06:42.569
<v Callum Reid>Exactly. I'll clear the jam and check the sensors; it matters, but it's not urgent.</v>

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:52.839
<v Grace Liu>I've got the line 3 barrel booking, too. Booking by the end of the week, not a promise of a contractor walking through the gate today.</v>

00:06:54.850 --> 00:07:01.149
<v Fiona Doyle>And the GT1 Fuel Gas Valve delivery remains unconfirmed. Nothing in this chat has unblocked the supplier side.</v>

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:04.420
<v Callum Reid>Correct. My sign-off doesn't change that delivery status.</v>

00:07:05.529 --> 00:07:13.230
<v David Whitfield>Lovely. And my Line 3 Screw and Barrel filter stays in the done column. I heard line 3 twice and got nervous.</v>

00:07:15.459 --> 00:07:18.610
<v Callum Reid>It stays done. We're not awarding you an encore.</v>

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:22.389
<v Priya Raman>That's unusually generous for a Friday.</v>

00:07:24.029 --> 00:07:25.779
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, all clear from me.</v>

00:07:26.139 --> 00:07:27.889
<v Callum Reid>Good. Thanks, everyone. That's us.</v>
